{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773178006,"nonce":"B8glK5aiNxlixrgHc+AQCwCGYFY=","title":"PenzaiSubgraph builder_name not persisted in graph_to_spec — round-trip crashes on deserialization","message":"graph_to_spec serializes PenzaiSubgraph as type \"PenzaiAdapter\" but writes no builder_name to the params dict (the comment in the code explicitly acknowledges this). spec_to_graph then requires builder_name to instantiate the Penzai model and raises ValueError without it. Fix: store builder_name as an attribute on the PenzaiSubgraph Python class at construction time, then read it in graph_to_spec and write it to serialized params. For legacy objects without the attribute, fall back gracefully.","files":null}]}